{"t": 16.88, "kind": "tool.result", "actor": "super", "tool": "start_helper", "args": {"title": "5-slide deck about Uruguay", "brief": "Build a 5-slide presentation deck about Uruguay and save it as a .pptx file in the current working directory (name it uruguay.pptx). Use a clean, modern design with a consistent color palette inspired by the Uruguayan flag (sky blue, white, gold sun accent). Each slide should have a clear title, concise bullet points (3\u20135 max), and at least one visual element (image, icon, map, or simple chart) where appropriate.\n\nSlides:\n1. Title slide \u2014 \"Uruguay\" with a subtitle (e.g., \"A Small Country with a Big Story\"), a flag or map visual.\n2. Geography & People \u2014 location in South America (between Argentina and Brazil, Atlantic coast), area ~176,000 km\u00b2, population ~3.4\u20133.5 million, capital Montevideo (about half the population), temperate climate, rolling grasslands (pampas).\n3. History & Government \u2014 independence 1825/1828 after the Cisplatine War, Jos\u00e9 Artigas as national hero, stable presidential democracy, early social reforms under Jos\u00e9 Batlle y Ord\u00f3\u00f1ez (8-hour workday, secular state, women's suffrage), military dictatorship 1973\u20131985 and return to democracy, former president Jos\u00e9 \"Pepe\" Mujica.\n4. Culture & Daily Life \u2014 mate culture, asado (beef barbecue), football (first World Cup host and winner in 1930, winners again in 1950), candombe and tango (Carnival in Montevideo is the longest in the world), literature (Mario Benedetti, Eduardo Galeano), high literacy and quality-of-life rankings.\n5. Economy & Modern Uruguay \u2014 agriculture exports (beef, soy, dairy, wool, pulp), strong renewable energy (~90%+ electricity from renewables, mostly wind/hydro), high GDP per capita for the region, progressive legislation (first country to fully legalize cannabis in 2013, same-sex marriage 2013), Punta del Este tourism, strong democratic and low-corruption rankings.\n\